1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:05,150
Never forget why you are the church.

2
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:16,750
Amen.

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,199
Go ahead and turn your Bibles to Romans chapter 12.

4
00:00:20,383 --> 00:00:22,149
Romans chapter 12.

5
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:26,533
This morning, we are moving right along through this 12th

6
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:32,283
chapter of Romans, looking at how we are to biblically respond to others.

7
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:40,799
We can say all the nice things that we want about each other, but what do your actions reveal regarding your relationships with others.

8
00:00:41,783 --> 00:00:46,500
These commands in this portion of text speaks primarily on reactions.

9
00:00:46,566 --> 00:00:49,866
Last week, we looked at the 1st one in Romans chapter

10
00:00:49,866 --> 00:00:56,399
12, verse 14, it says this, the less than which persecutes you, bless and curse not.

11
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:58,383
Let me read that again.

12
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,366
Bless them which persecutes you.

13
00:01:00,983 --> 00:01:03,366
Bless and curse not.

14
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,966
Are you someone who blesses or curses?

15
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:11,650
Well, you don't know what they did or what they said or you don't

16
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:13,266
really know really what you're talking about.

17
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:14,400
I want to clarify something here.

18
00:01:14,466 --> 00:01:19,266
Nowhere in scripture is sin ever justified or tolerated.

19
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:22,866
Just because there's sin in scripture,

20
00:01:22,866 --> 00:01:26,283
just because there's people of God who have sinned that

21
00:01:26,283 --> 00:01:31,916
is recorded in the text does not mean that God ever justified or tolerated that sin.

22
00:01:32,049 --> 00:01:37,016
The sinner may try to do so, but God's holiness does not and will not allow it.

23
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:38,633
So I don't want you to miss that.

24
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:44,700
That being true, what someone has done to us does not give us the right to curse them.

25
00:01:48,333 --> 00:01:53,033
Listen, just because someone's done something, doesn't mean that what they have done to us isn't wrong.

26
00:01:53,983 --> 00:01:56,533
Doesn't mean that someone has not abused this.

27
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:59,099
It doesn't mean that someone has not done a bad thing.

28
00:01:59,166 --> 00:02:03,299
What I'm trying to say is our biblical reaction is

29
00:02:03,299 --> 00:02:06,416
based on scripture and God's word, not our feelings.

30
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:09,433
Now, what does it look like to curse someone?

31
00:02:09,483 --> 00:02:12,599
Remember the meaning, to curse, pronounce, a curse upon, refers

32
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:16,133
to the act of pronouncing misfortune for someone else.

33
00:02:17,483 --> 00:02:21,900
Do you understand the depth of this command, even when someone is directly attacking you?

34
00:02:21,966 --> 00:02:25,083
And by the way, we talked at length last week about how

35
00:02:25,083 --> 00:02:28,133
a lot of these things that we talk about is a direct attack

36
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:31,983
on us and, oh, preacher, I'm going through persecutions, that's not a persecution.

37
00:02:32,050 --> 00:02:32,883
That's just an off day.

38
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:37,083
Persecution is leaving the house and having someone literally

39
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:41,699
because of your faith, going after you, intentionally and nonstop.

40
00:02:41,766 --> 00:02:45,183
That's what Timothy saw or that's what, sorry, Stephen saw in scripture.

41
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,949
That's what Jesus saw when he was here on his earth.

42
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:51,783
But it's someone making their mission to hurt you.

43
00:02:51,849 --> 00:02:54,066
It's not that you don't handle business and protect yourself.

44
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:58,250
Rather, you make sure you can never be found lowering yourself to their level.

45
00:02:58,333 --> 00:02:59,949
Blessed, do not curse.

46
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:02,766
We moved this morning to the next one.

47
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:03,783
Romans 12, verse 15.

48
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:04,633
It says this.

49
00:03:04,683 --> 00:03:08,583
Rejoice with them that do rejoice and weep with them.

50
00:03:09,133 --> 00:03:09,783
that weep.

51
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:13,266
Last week, we looked at the power of persecution.

52
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,849
Why was that the title?

53
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:16,616
Well, think about it.

54
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,266
If you are truly getting persecuted.

55
00:03:20,483 --> 00:03:22,449
And you respond with blessing and not cursing.

56
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,216
Let me just tell you something.

57
00:03:23,883 --> 00:03:24,849
That's going to be noticed.

58
00:03:26,483 --> 00:03:28,933
Everybody in the world curses those who curse them.

59
00:03:29,983 --> 00:03:33,366
Everybody in the world, when someone does someone wrong, they lash

60
00:03:33,366 --> 00:03:36,666
out and they say this, they say that, but man, when a believer,

61
00:03:36,666 --> 00:03:39,716
even though they're getting persecuted, speaks highly of

62
00:03:39,733 --> 00:03:42,733
this person, not of what they've done, but says, hey, God loves you.

63
00:03:42,783 --> 00:03:44,216
I forgive you, all the things.

64
00:03:44,283 --> 00:03:45,716
Man, that is noticed.

65
00:03:45,783 --> 00:03:47,816
That is a testimony right in of itself.

66
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:54,300
So there's power in persecution, but also this week we're going to look at the power of empathy.

67
00:03:55,183 --> 00:03:56,233
The power of empathy.

68
00:03:56,283 --> 00:03:56,699
Let's pray.

69
00:03:56,766 --> 00:03:57,833
Father, I thank you for this morning.

70
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,633
I thank you, God, for this gathering.

71
00:04:00,483 --> 00:04:02,949
So Lord, allow me to preach, God, with power and clarity.

72
00:04:04,183 --> 00:04:05,833
Well, God, I pray those that have ears to hear.

73
00:04:05,883 --> 00:04:06,300
May they hear.

74
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:07,866
In Jesus name, pray.

75
00:04:07,933 --> 00:04:08,533
Amen.

76
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:11,583
There are many issues with the church today.

77
00:04:12,983 --> 00:04:14,650
But I'm not stating that as others do.

78
00:04:14,699 --> 00:04:17,100
A lot of people like to beat up on the bride.

79
00:04:18,233 --> 00:04:20,583
A lot of people like to beat up on the local church.

80
00:04:20,649 --> 00:04:23,649
A lot of people like to get on social media and give their

81
00:04:23,649 --> 00:04:28,016
opinion about why the church isn't what it needs to be and this and that, blah, blah, blah.

82
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:31,333
I believe that the church is a beautiful and biblical thing.

83
00:04:31,383 --> 00:04:34,500
I believe the church is full of broken yet restored people who

84
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:38,399
come together with the same purpose and intention of honoring God together.

85
00:04:38,466 --> 00:04:40,733
Now, that's not obviously everybody.

86
00:04:41,483 --> 00:04:43,800
But why let the fake ones take away from the real ones.

87
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:44,216
Amen?

88
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:48,550
Well, preacher, I think I'll just have church at my house with a select

89
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:51,550
few, and we'll just kind of do what we want to do.

90
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:55,366
Well, let me just, if your goal is discipleship, then I'm all the way in.

91
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,600
We would call that a small group.

92
00:04:57,666 --> 00:04:58,016
Amen?

93
00:04:58,683 --> 00:05:04,250
We would call bringing a few people into your home and discipling them and teaching the Bible.

94
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:05,350
There's nothing wrong with that.

95
00:05:05,399 --> 00:05:08,566
Jesus preached to the masses and he discipled a few.

96
00:05:08,649 --> 00:05:11,466
That is a biblical and successful model.

97
00:05:11,533 --> 00:05:14,583
However, if you do this so that you can make

98
00:05:14,583 --> 00:05:16,683
the rules and everything can be on your terms.

99
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,300
You aren't having church.

100
00:05:21,533 --> 00:05:25,083
You're doing exactly what you accuse the local church down the street of doing.

101
00:05:25,983 --> 00:05:27,066
Making the rules.

102
00:05:28,983 --> 00:05:31,266
Don't come to me thinking you can do better than everybody else.

103
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:35,649
It's easy to sit back and say, oh, well, I'd have done that.

104
00:05:35,699 --> 00:05:36,166
I would have done this.

105
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:36,666
Well, guess what?

106
00:05:36,733 --> 00:05:37,266
Something got done.

107
00:05:37,333 --> 00:05:37,933
It wasn't by you.

108
00:05:41,283 --> 00:05:46,800
See, even with the flaws, the local church is a force for good that must not be taken for granted.

109
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:51,300
Now, one of these many issues that I alluded to is derived

110
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:56,399
from the principles found in verse 15, the church, I believe, has lost its empathy.

111
00:05:57,533 --> 00:05:59,350
Now, what does it mean to have empathy?

112
00:05:59,466 --> 00:06:02,466
Empathy is the capacity to feel another

113
00:06:02,466 --> 00:06:05,633
person's feelings, thoughts, or attitudes vicariously.

114
00:06:06,533 --> 00:06:09,483
Now, empathy is not to be mistaken with sympathy.

115
00:06:09,550 --> 00:06:14,033
Now, sympathy, and I'm talking about how the world sees and how the world defines these, right?

116
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:18,533
Sympathy is having compassion and pity from an outside perspective.

117
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:23,050
Empathy brings you inside with the person in

118
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:25,616
order to walk with them through their hurt or their joy.

119
00:06:26,583 --> 00:06:30,433
I'll give you an example, and then we'll break down the 2 phrases here in verse 15.

120
00:06:31,533 --> 00:06:34,800
Sympathy is seeing that same Facebook post and

121
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:37,966
messaging them with the intention of stepping or, I'm

122
00:06:37,983 --> 00:06:42,716
sorry, sympathy is seeing a Facebook post and someone going through something sad.

123
00:06:42,783 --> 00:06:48,899
We see it all the time on Facebook and out of sympathy, you click the care emoji or you

124
00:06:48,899 --> 00:06:53,333
click the little heart emoji and you might even you might even comment, oh, praying for you.

125
00:06:53,399 --> 00:06:54,166
That's sympathy.

126
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:56,350
That is seeing a need and being sad from afar.

127
00:06:57,433 --> 00:07:00,966
Empathy is seeing that same message, direct

128
00:07:00,966 --> 00:07:03,183
message and saying, hey, listen, how can I help you?

129
00:07:03,250 --> 00:07:04,683
How can I walk with you through this?

130
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:07,750
How can I, how can I be there for you?

131
00:07:07,866 --> 00:07:11,166
Sympathy is thinking about someone in the hospital suffering?

132
00:07:11,233 --> 00:07:12,966
Man, I can't believe they're at the hospital.

133
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:14,350
I can't believe they had to go.

134
00:07:14,399 --> 00:07:15,600
They've been there for 3 or 4 days.

135
00:07:15,666 --> 00:07:18,716
Empathy is going and sitting with them during their suffering.

136
00:07:19,983 --> 00:07:22,333
Sympathy is actual concern, but from a distance.

137
00:07:23,183 --> 00:07:26,050
Empathy is concerned, it turns into action.

138
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:29,050
If you want to write anything down, write this down.

139
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:32,933
Sympathy is feeling for, Empathy is feeling with.

140
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:36,899
Sympathy is feeling for empathy is filling with.

141
00:07:36,966 --> 00:07:37,800
Everyone with me so far.

142
00:07:39,233 --> 00:07:43,033
Now, Paul here starts this verse by saying, rejoice with them that do rejoice.

143
00:07:44,033 --> 00:07:47,399
Now, most think that epathy is only for bad situations,

144
00:07:47,399 --> 00:07:51,833
but here we see that we are to walk with others even in their triumphs.

145
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:56,050
I'm gonna say something that may sound incorrect, but if we're honest, we know it to be true.

146
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,416
Let me hit you with this.

147
00:07:58,383 --> 00:08:01,449
It is more difficult to celebrate with others in their good

148
00:08:01,449 --> 00:08:04,866
times than to suffer with others in their bad times.

149
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:07,333
You know with me?

150
00:08:08,183 --> 00:08:08,949
Let me explain that.

151
00:08:09,633 --> 00:08:12,966
It is more difficult to celebrate with others in their successes

152
00:08:12,966 --> 00:08:16,800
and their victories than it is when they're going through a hard time.

153
00:08:18,783 --> 00:08:20,283
What could possibly cause this?

154
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:21,600
Well, pride?

155
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:25,683
Ego, jealousy, covishness, laziness.

156
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:28,800
They have what you desire, so instead of rejoicing with

157
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,633
them, you would rather nitpick and superficially congratulate them, and

158
00:08:32,649 --> 00:08:35,766
then move on as fast as possible, not thinking about what God has blessed them with.

159
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:38,950
Someone's business grows exponentially.

160
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,633
Someone's family expands, the young couple builds their dream home.

161
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:43,733
Your coworker friend gets that promotion.

162
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:48,666
Listen, if you don't think that pastors deal with this, you're out of your stinking mind.

163
00:08:50,483 --> 00:08:51,783
Listen, it's very easy.

164
00:08:51,850 --> 00:08:53,649
Comparison is the thief of joy.

165
00:08:54,433 --> 00:08:57,183
And we live in a county that has a lot of good growing churches.

166
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:00,366
And I can tell you right now, it's easy sometimes to compare,

167
00:09:00,366 --> 00:09:02,700
the church down the street hits record attendance.

168
00:09:02,766 --> 00:09:05,933
The church of a similar size, they able to operate with double the budget.

169
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:10,616
The church in town and seeing their programs grow and thrive and see what the flesh wants to do.

170
00:09:10,683 --> 00:09:11,816
The flesh wants to downplay it.

171
00:09:11,950 --> 00:09:12,966
we'll see.

172
00:09:13,033 --> 00:09:13,750
They just started it.

173
00:09:13,799 --> 00:09:15,166
It won't be successful for long.

174
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,166
It probably won't continue.

175
00:09:17,233 --> 00:09:18,733
Well, I didn't want that promotion anyway.

176
00:09:18,783 --> 00:09:21,299
They are crazy to building this economy.

177
00:09:24,366 --> 00:09:27,716
I want to give you 2 points to remember when it comes to rejoicing with those who rejoice.

178
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,783
First off, what you rejoice about reveals your heart posture.

179
00:09:32,533 --> 00:09:35,833
If you can rejoice with someone, even in their victories, what you're

180
00:09:35,833 --> 00:09:39,600
saying is, listen, I'm living in humility, and you'll win is a win for me.

181
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:41,700
Can I tell you something?

182
00:09:41,766 --> 00:09:44,100
People say, hey, listen, I don't think people should be rich.

183
00:09:45,633 --> 00:09:46,983
I don't think money's a bad thing.

184
00:09:49,183 --> 00:09:51,133
I think the love of money is the root of all evil.

185
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,433
I think we are to use money, not money use us.

186
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:56,283
Does that make sense?

187
00:09:56,350 --> 00:09:58,016
And let me just tell you something.

188
00:09:58,083 --> 00:10:02,149
Somebody that makes a lot of money is very well off.

189
00:10:02,233 --> 00:10:04,983
Listen, they can do things that other people may not be able to do.

190
00:10:05,049 --> 00:10:05,816
That's a win.

191
00:10:08,033 --> 00:10:10,500
So all I'm trying to say is we should celebrate that.

192
00:10:11,783 --> 00:10:12,966
Our heart posture.

193
00:10:13,033 --> 00:10:13,750
What is a second?

194
00:10:13,799 --> 00:10:15,766
Fake rejoicing is easy to spot.

195
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:20,766
Have you ever fake rejoiced over something that you didn't really want to rejoice over?

196
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:23,049
It's like, oh, I'm so happy for you.

197
00:10:27,383 --> 00:10:28,500
Thank you for sharing that.

198
00:10:28,566 --> 00:10:30,299
I'm so glad that happened to you.

199
00:10:32,583 --> 00:10:33,533
Listen, we do it all time.

200
00:10:34,683 --> 00:10:36,433
You may think you are good at hiding it.

201
00:10:36,483 --> 00:10:38,033
Your pride and jealousy, but you are not.

202
00:10:38,166 --> 00:10:39,183
many people have this mindset.

203
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:41,700
You know the song, The Lord bless you.

204
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:43,566
Unless he blesses you more than me.

205
00:10:45,383 --> 00:10:46,933
And keep you.

206
00:10:46,983 --> 00:10:49,133
Make his face shine upon you.

207
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,166
Just not as bright as he's shining on me.

208
00:10:53,583 --> 00:10:54,600
Think about it for a second.

209
00:10:54,666 --> 00:10:57,966
Listen, I know it's silly, but that's how we live our life oftentimes.

210
00:10:59,433 --> 00:11:02,100
It's really cool until someone gets something that we wanted.

211
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:06,783
What a meansable way to live, amen?

212
00:11:08,383 --> 00:11:12,299
Now, you may be thinking that this has been a lot of opinion rather than scripture.

213
00:11:12,433 --> 00:11:16,683
And, you know, hey, listen, any opinion I have, I pray that I base it on scripture.

214
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:17,049
Amen.

215
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:18,950
So is there an example of this in the Bible?

216
00:11:19,033 --> 00:11:19,683
Well, you know it is.

217
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:20,700
I wouldn't be saying this stuff.

218
00:11:20,766 --> 00:11:21,966
Remember King Saul.

219
00:11:22,633 --> 00:11:24,250
The 1st king of Israel.

220
00:11:24,299 --> 00:11:25,433
How does scripture describe this man?

221
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:27,166
First Samuel 9, verse 2 says this.

222
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:30,299
He had a son whose name was Saul, a choice and

223
00:11:30,299 --> 00:11:33,350
handsome man, and there was not a more handsome person than

224
00:11:33,366 --> 00:11:36,600
he among the sons of Israel from his shoulders and up.

225
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:39,299
He was taller than any of the people.

226
00:11:39,883 --> 00:11:43,566
This dude, physically, was seemingly the perfect fit for a king.

227
00:11:43,633 --> 00:11:47,399
Early on, he had experienced some pretty significant wins.

228
00:11:47,466 --> 00:11:50,283
He united the scattered 12 tribes.

229
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:53,100
He established the military and administrative state.

230
00:11:53,166 --> 00:11:56,766
He led early Israelite forces through critical battlefield victories.

231
00:11:56,833 --> 00:12:00,066
I mean, King Saul was making it happen as king.

232
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:03,133
He was on top of the world.

233
00:12:03,883 --> 00:12:05,233
Nobody could beat him.

234
00:12:05,883 --> 00:12:08,399
Then this young shepherd boy named David arrived.

235
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:12,549
See, David, at a young age, was no had no experience

236
00:12:12,549 --> 00:12:16,866
of ruling, but he had a boldness and a courage that Saul did not have.

237
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:20,766
David was displayed, he displayed a faith

238
00:12:20,766 --> 00:12:24,183
in God that exposed Saul's lack of faith in God.

239
00:12:25,033 --> 00:12:28,033
It was David who slew Goliath while Saul sat

240
00:12:28,033 --> 00:12:31,149
back and allowed the enemy to blaspheme the name of God.

241
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:34,666
It was David who became known as a mighty warrior.

242
00:12:34,750 --> 00:12:37,450
As a matter of fact, in 1st Samuel 18, 5 and 7.

243
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,033
